@cecrevier 

SCTP kernel driver provide SHUTDOWN or COMM_LOST event to the MME. There are related parameters in Open5GS.

See the src/mme/s1ap-sctp.c:166

```
           } else if (not->sn_assoc_change.sac_state == SCTP_SHUTDOWN_COMP ||
                    not->sn_assoc_change.sac_state == SCTP_COMM_LOST) {

                if (not->sn_assoc_change.sac_state == SCTP_SHUTDOWN_COMP)
                    ogs_debug("SCTP_SHUTDOWN_COMP");
                if (not->sn_assoc_change.sac_state == SCTP_COMM_LOST)
                    ogs_debug("SCTP_COMM_LOST");

                addr = ogs_calloc(1, sizeof(ogs_sockaddr_t));
                ogs_assert(addr);
                memcpy(addr, &from, sizeof(ogs_sockaddr_t));

                s1ap_event_push(MME_EVT_S1AP_LO_CONNREFUSED,
                        sock, addr, NULL, 0, 0);
            }
            break;

```

And also, you can change the mme.yaml like the followings.
```
#
# sctp:
#
#  o heartbit_interval : 5000 (5secs)
#  o rto_initial : 3000 (3secs)
#  o rto_min : 1000 (1sec)
#  o rto_max : 5000 (5secs)
#  o max_num_of_ostreams : 30
#  o max_num_of_istreams : 65535
#  o max_attempts : 4
#  o max_initial_timeout : 8000(8secs)
#  o usrsctp_udp_port : 9899
#
sctp:
    heartbit_interval : 30000
    rto_initial : 3000 
    rto_min : 1000 
    rto_max : 60000
```

However, I don't know the parameters related to satellite delay. And, I am not sure if modifying the parameters will solve the problem.

Thank you for sharing your environment.
Sukchan

